From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:34:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: add the MO6TWPC instruction set

TYN-only: the Windows/Steam release of Memories Off 6 T-Wave uses the
MO8/CHN generation SC3 dialect, not the PS3 MO6TW one. Add
InstructionSet::MO6TWPC with its own opcode table (opcodetables_mo6twpc.h),
copied from MO8 with these changes:
  - 00:5A: InstUnk005APC, one u16 operand, stub. Evidence from the
    disassembly of the PC scripts: _system label 1 contains
    `00 5a 59 00` followed by `01 02 ...`; with a u16 operand (0x0059) the
    stream continues at `01 02` and the label decodes cleanly through to its
    Return. The meaning of the operand is unknown.
  - 10:0F: InstUnk100FPC, a zero-operand stub (MO8 has InstDummy, which never
    advances the IP and hangs the thread). The disassembler shows 10:0F is
    followed directly by the next opcode (38 uses).
  - 10:1A: InstHelp (u8), as in CC/LCCSwitch. 10:1B stays InstHelp (also
    used by PC scripts).
  - Every opcode that has no handler maps to InstDummyPC instead of InstDummy.
    Semantics are the same (does nothing, does not advance the IP, so a
    script that executes one hangs), but it logs an Error once per opcode
    with group:op, script buffer and address, so such a hang is visible in
    the log. InstDummy itself (used by the other sets) is untouched.
  - Unpinned dummies 00:EC/58/F8/4C: at the failing sites the bytes are label
    tables (u16/u32 label lists after Return/End) and data after a
    JumpTable, not instructions, so no handler is mapped for them.

Every existing GameInstructionSet == MO8 check also accepts MO6TWPC:
  - inst_dialogue.cpp InstSel (SelInit savepoint id), InstNameID (name plate
    label), InstTips (extra local label)
  - inst_misc.cpp InstTitleMenuNew (the MO8 case), InstSetEVflag (extra u8)
  - inst_sound.cpp InstSysSeload (extra u8)
  - character2d.cpp base-size scale / rotation branch
  - game.cpp movie priority render special case
InstClistInit type 0x14 (PC only) takes one expression operand and is
stubbed. (src/profile/games/mo8, src/games/mo8 and the UI enums are
profile-type based, not instruction-set based, and are untouched.)

Disassembler (modelled operand shapes) decodes 3830 label bodies with the
new table, identical to the MO8 table + PC patches.

